41:["$","$L53",null,{"type":"multiple","children":[["$","$L54",null,{"title":"My store builds with Cargo but CI fails. Why?","id":"cargo-green-bazel-red","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Almost certainly the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"srcs"}]," list in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-store/BUILD.bazel"}],". Cargo\nglobs; Bazel enumerates. Add the file, keep the list alphabetical, and\nrun ",["$","code",null,{"children":"bazel build //forge-store:forge-store"}]," before pushing."]}]}],["$","$L54",null,{"title":"My new config field doesn't show up in the reference.","id":"field-missing-from-reference","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Check that the spec struct has\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"#[cfg_attr(feature = \"dev-schema\", derive(JsonSchema))]"}],". The generated\nreference is produced from the schemars schema, and a struct without that\nderive is invisible to it. If the field is there but has no default,\nadd a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/// Default: …"}]," line to the doc comment."]}]}],["$","$L54",null,{"title":"A doc comment broke the build. How?","id":"doc-comment-broke-build","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Doc comments in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-config"}]," are load-bearing twice over: fenced\nJSON blocks are extracted into\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-config/examples/stores-config.json5"}]," by a pre-commit hook,\nand ",["$","code",null,{"children":"tests/json5_test.rs"}]," parses every generated example. Malformed JSON\nin a fence fails that test."]}]}],["$","$L54",null,{"title":"Do I need protoc installed to add a proto?","id":"need-protoc","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["No. Generated Rust is checked into ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-proto/genproto/"}],", and\nregeneration goes through ",["$","code",null,{"children":"bazel run forge-proto:update_protos"}],".\nCommit the regenerated files with your change."]}]}],["$","$L54",null,{"title":"Where does a new store's default go?","id":"where-do-store-defaults-go","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["In the implementation, not the config crate; the spec should describe\nintent, and the store applies its own fallback. Record the value in the\nfield's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/// Default:"}]," line so the reference stays honest."]}]}]]}]
